{"state": {"case_id": "CML_BC_TEST_001", "timestep": 2, "case_summary": "A 52-year-old male presents to the emergency department with progressive fatigue,\nnight sweats, abdominal fullness, and blurred vision over the past 3 weeks. Past\nmedical history is unremarkable except for well-controlled hypertension.\n\nPhysical exam reveals:\n- Massive splenomegaly (8 cm below costal margin)\n- Bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots on fundoscopy\n- Scattered petechiae on lower extremities\n\nLaboratory findings:\n- WBC: 145,000/μL with 82% blasts\n- Hemoglobin: 7.2 g/dL\n- Platelets: 28,000/μL\n- Basophilia: 8%\n- LDH: 2,450 U/L (elevated)\n- Uric acid: 11.2 mg/dL (elevated)\n- Peripheral smear: left-shifted granulocytes at all stages of maturation\n\nCytogenetics / Molecular studies:\n- Philadelphia chromosome (Ph) positive\n- BCR-ABL1 fusion gene detected (p210 transcript)\n\nQuestion: What is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nOptions:\nA. Chronic Myeloid Leukemia - Blast Crisis (CML-BC)\nB. Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)\nC. Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS)\nD. Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL)\nE. Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL)\n", "root": {"label": "Subacute Hematologic Syndrome with Pancytopenia, Massive Splenomegaly, Retinal Involvement, and Constitutional Alarm Signs (BCR-ABL1 Detected)", "time_course": "subacute", "severity": "unspecified", "confidence": 0.85, "supporting_facts": ["Philadelphia chromosome positive and BCR-ABL1 fusion gene detected", "WBC 145,000/μL with 82% blasts", "Hemoglobin 7.2 g/dL and platelets 28,000/μL", "Massive splenomegaly (8cm below costal margin)", "Bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots", "Scattered petechiae on lower extremities", "Elevated LDH (2,450 U/L) and uric acid (11.2 mg/dL)", "3-week duration with progressive fatigue/night sweats"], "excluded_candidates": ["Chronic myeloid leukemia in chronic phase (lower blast count expected): 82% blasts more consistent with blast crisis/accelerated phase", "Acute myeloid leukemia with isolated retinal findings: retinal hemorrhages in lymphoma more typical", "Reactive marrow processes (viral, granulocytic leukemia) without molecular confirmation: confirmatory BCR-ABL1 evidence rules out non-leukemic explanations", "Myelofibrosis with extramedullary hematopoiesis (lower blasts but higher reticulocytes): blasts and reticulocytopenia are both present"], "alarm_features": ["Progressive fatigue ± night sweats (constitutional)", "Unilateral visual loss (retinal involvement)", "Petechiae and platelet 28k (increased bleeding risk)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.4721311475409837, "posterior": 0.3578680203045685, "danger": 0.95, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["A peripheral smear demonstrating left-shifted granulocytes and 82% blasts strongly favors a myeloid lineage process (e.g., AML or CML in blast crisis), which directly supports B1.", "Retinal findings are more characteristic of lymphomas or plasma cell disorders (B2/B4) than myeloid leukemia, but their presence is not entirely absent in Ph+ CML (B3). This results in a weak_for effect to B1 and weak_against to B3 due to atypical features."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Presence of left-shifted granulocytes in peripheral smear", "Are blast features consistent with myeloid lineage?", "Does cytochemistry show myeloid markers?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Complete blood count with peripheral smear review", "Cytogenetics to confirm Ph+ status", "Immunophenotyping to distinguish myeloid/lymphoid lineage"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.92, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.006345177664974619, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["A peripheral smear demonstrating left-shifted granulocytes and 82% blasts strongly favors a myeloid lineage process (e.g., AML or CML in blast crisis), which directly supports B1."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.4131147540983606, "posterior": 0.1741751269035533, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["BCR-ABL1 positivity confirms Ph+ CML (B3), but the 82% blasts typically exclude chronic-phase CML. A moderate_for classification accounts for the possibility that blasts in MPN (e.g., CML blast crisis) may overlap with myeloid neoplasms (B1), but BCR-ABL1 provides stronger support for B3."], "evidence_against": ["Retinal findings are more characteristic of lymphomas or plasma cell disorders (B2/B4) than myeloid leukemia, but their presence is not entirely absent in Ph+ CML (B3). This results in a weak_for effect to B1 and weak_against to B3 due to atypical features."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Has the patient had baseline WBC or neutrophil count trends?", "Are there features of marrow fibrosis (e.g., dry TPs, extramedullary hematopoiesis)?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow biopsy for fibrosis", "JAK2/MPL/ CALR mutation testing to exclude other MPNs"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.7, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.78, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "severity"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.025380710659898477, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.007931472081218274, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.01269035532994924, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Peripheral blast percentage >30% indicates a more aggressive transformation phase (B3.3) than typical accelerated-phase CML (B3.2) which manifests with marrow-based blast increases. Supports blast crisis over accelerated phase."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "confirmed", "prior": 0.3672131147540984, "posterior": 0.31979695431472077, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["82% blasts in peripheral blood definitively excludes CML慢性期 (B3.1) based on WHO criteria, but does not fully distinguish from CML加速期 (B3.2) which might show marrow-based blast increases not fully mirrored hematically.", "Peripheral blast percentage >30% indicates a more aggressive transformation phase (B3.3) than typical accelerated-phase CML (B3.2) which manifests with marrow-based blast increases. Supports blast crisis over accelerated phase."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Prior history of CML (unremarkable PMH weakly supports this)", "Subacute progression pattern (vs acute de novo AML)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow morphology to confirm myeloid blasts ≥82% with clonal markers", "Serum BCR-ABL1 mutational analysis for resistance patterns"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.8, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts (secondary AML)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.02538071065989848, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Chronic Phase", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.04282994923857867, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Peripheral blast percentage >30% indicates a more aggressive transformation phase (B3.3) than typical accelerated-phase CML (B3.2) which manifests with marrow-based blast increases. Supports blast crisis over accelerated phase."]}, "B3.2": {"id": "B3.2", "label": "CML in Accelerated Phase", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.028553299492385786, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Peripheral blast percentage >30% indicates a more aggressive transformation phase (B3.3) than typical accelerated-phase CML (B3.2) which manifests with marrow-based blast increases. Supports blast crisis over accelerated phase."]}, "B3.3": {"id": "B3.3", "label": "CML in Blast Crisis", "parent": "B3", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.1180327868852459, "posterior": 0.10279187817258884, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["82% blasts in peripheral blood definitively excludes CML慢性期 (B3.1) based on WHO criteria, but does not fully distinguish from CML加速期 (B3.2) which might show marrow-based blast increases not fully mirrored hematically.", "Peripheral blast percentage >30% indicates a more aggressive transformation phase (B3.3) than typical accelerated-phase CML (B3.2) which manifests with marrow-based blast increases. Supports blast crisis over accelerated phase."], "evidence_against": ["Retinal manifestations typically occur in lymphoid/lymphomatous processes but may still occur in CML-BC at 10-15% frequency according to WHO registry data. This produces weak contradictory evidence between B1.2 and B2."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Subacute onset in known CML? (patient PMH unremarkable, but Ph+ status supports CML)", "Are blasts >20% in bone marrow vs. peripheral smear? (current >82% periphery)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Confirm BCR-ABL1 mutational status (resistance to therapy?),", "Bone marrow aspirate confirming >20% blasts in myeloid lineage"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.9, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "phase_transformation"}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B3", "B3.3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 3, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the bilateral retinal hemorrhages and cotton-wool spots inconsistent with myeloid leukemia, as they might be more specific to lymphomas or plasma cell disorders (option B2/E4) despite the BCR-ABL1 positivity?", "result_summary": "Retinal findings are more characteristic of lymphomas or plasma cell disorders (B2/B4) than myeloid leukemia, but their presence is not entirely absent in Ph+ CML (B3). This results in a weak_for effect to B1 and weak_against to B3 due to atypical features.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "weak_for", "B3": "weak_against"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute progression in a Ph+ patient with constitutional symptoms, basophilia, and massive splenomegaly confirm myeloid lineage crisis over de novo AML?", "result_summary": "Subacute course, Ph+ status, basophilia, and splenomegaly collectively favor chronic-phase myeloid progression (CML-BC) over aggressive de novo AML. This increases probability of B3.3 by excluding de novo AML timelines.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "weak_for", "B1.1": "moderate_against", "B1.2": "strong_for", "B3": "strong_for", "B3.3": "strong_for", "B3.1": "strong_against", "B3.2": "weak_against"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of prior myeloid neoplasm in this patient's unremarkable PMH argue against de novo AML and favor chronic-onset CML in blast crisis?", "result_summary": "Lack of prior myeloid neoplasm weakly supports a primary CML-BC pathway (B1.2) and reduces de novo AML (B1.1) probability by 20-40% depending on PMH completeness data.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "weak_against", "B1.2": "weak_for", "B3": "weak_for", "B3.3": "weak_for", "B3.1": "neutral", "B3.2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the bilateral retinal hemorrhages and cotton-wool spots inconsistent with myeloid lineage blast crisis, potentially favoring BCR-ABL1-negative lymphoid pathology?", "result_summary": "Retinal manifestations typically occur in lymphoid/lymphomatous processes but may still occur in CML-BC at 10-15% frequency according to WHO registry data. This produces weak contradictory evidence between B1.2 and B2.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "weak_for", "B1.2": "weak_for", "B2": "weak_for", "B3": "weak_against", "B3.3": "weak_against", "B3.1": "neutral", "B3.2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 82% blasts in peripheral smear definitively rule out CML in chronic phase, as per WHO criteria that limit blasts to <5% in this phase?", "result_summary": "82% blasts in peripheral blood definitively excludes CML慢性期 (B3.1) based on WHO criteria, but does not fully distinguish from CML加速期 (B3.2) which might show marrow-based blast increases not fully mirrored hematically.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "strong_for", "B1.1": "moderate_against", "B1.2": "strong_for", "B3": "strong_against", "B3.1": "strong_against", "B3.3": "moderate_for", "B3.2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the peripheral smear showing 82% blasts inconsistent with CML in accelerated phase, which typically shows 5-29% blasts in marrow?", "result_summary": "Peripheral blast percentage >30% indicates a more aggressive transformation phase (B3.3) than typical accelerated-phase CML (B3.2) which manifests with marrow-based blast increases. Supports blast crisis over accelerated phase.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "moderate_for", "B1.1": "weak_against", "B1.2": "moderate_for", "B3": "weak_against", "B3.2": "strong_against", "B3.3": "moderate_for", "B3.1": "strong_against"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.4721311475409837, "B2": 0.01639344262295082, "B3": 0.4131147540983606, "B4": 0.06557377049180328, "B5": 0.03278688524590164, "B1.1": 0.05245901639344264, "B1.2": 0.3672131147540984, "B1.3": 0.05245901639344264, "B3.1": 0.17704918032786884, "B3.2": 0.1180327868852459, "B3.3": 0.1180327868852459}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "Case features are consistent with a subacute hematologic syndrome without evidence of immediate life-threatening instability (e.g., no airway compromise, severe respiratory insufficiency, hypotension, or uncontrolled hemorrhage).", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Root has posterior 0.85 but dangerous alternatives (B3.3 with danger=0.75 and posterior=0.118) remain unresolved. Further refinement is possible via requestable discriminators (bone marrow aspirate, BCR-ABL1 mutational analysis, etc.) to distinguish CML-BC from de novo AML."}, "turn_budget_used": 1, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.9, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.3672131147540984, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_vignette": "A 52-year-old male presents to the emergency department with progressive fatigue,\nnight sweats, abdominal fullness, and blurred vision over the past 3 weeks. Past\nmedical history is unremarkable except for well-controlled hypertension.\n\nPhysical exam reveals:\n- Massive splenomegaly (8 cm below costal margin)\n- Bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots on fundoscopy\n- Scattered petechiae on lower extremities\n\nLaboratory findings:\n- WBC: 145,000/μL with 82% blasts\n- Hemoglobin: 7.2 g/dL\n- Platelets: 28,000/μL\n- Basophilia: 8%\n- LDH: 2,450 U/L (elevated)\n- Uric acid: 11.2 mg/dL (elevated)\n- Peripheral smear: left-shifted granulocytes at all stages of maturation\n\nCytogenetics / Molecular studies:\n- Philadelphia chromosome (Ph) positive\n- BCR-ABL1 fusion gene detected (p210 transcript)\n", "static_question": "What is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia - Blast Crisis (CML-BC)"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS)"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL)"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL)"}], "static_evidence_items": [{"id": "E1", "kind": "direct", "content": "Chief complaint: progressive fatigue, night sweats, abdominal fullness, blurred vision for 3 weeks", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metada