eukemia with isolated retinal findings: retinal hemorrhages in lymphoma more typical", "Reactive marrow processes (viral, granulocytic leukemia) without molecular confirmation: confirmatory BCR-ABL1 evidence rules out non-leukemic explanations", "Myelofibrosis with extramedullary hematopoiesis (lower blasts but higher reticulocytes): blasts and reticulocytopenia are both present"], "alarm_features": ["Progressive fatigue ± night sweats (constitutional)", "Unilateral visual loss (retinal involvement)", "Petechiae and platelet 28k (increased bleeding risk)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3578680203045685, "posterior": 0.28774464717881787, "danger": 0.95, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["A peripheral smear demonstrating left-shifted granulocytes and 82% blasts strongly favors a myeloid lineage process (e.g., AML or CML in blast crisis), which directly supports B1.", "Retinal findings are more characteristic of lymphomas or plasma cell disorders (B2/B4) than myeloid leukemia, but their presence is not entirely absent in Ph+ CML (B3). This results in a weak_for effect to B1 and weak_against to B3 due to atypical features."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Presence of left-shifted granulocytes in peripheral smear", "Are blast features consistent with myeloid lineage?", "Does cytochemistry show myeloid markers?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Complete blood count with peripheral smear review", "Cytogenetics to confirm Ph+ status", "Immunophenotyping to distinguish myeloid/lymphoid lineage"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.92, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.004110637816840256, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The Ph+ status combined with subacute pancytopenia suggests a transformation phase rather than a mixed lineage crisis, providing moderate evidence for CML-BC."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.1741751269035533, "posterior": 0.16708201236274325, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["BCR-ABL1 positivity confirms Ph+ CML (B3), but the 82% blasts typically exclude chronic-phase CML. A moderate_for classification accounts for the possibility that blasts in MPN (e.g., CML blast crisis) may overlap with myeloid neoplasms (B1), but BCR-ABL1 provides stronger support for B3."], "evidence_against": ["Retinal findings are more characteristic of lymphomas or plasma cell disorders (B2/B4) than myeloid leukemia, but their presence is not entirely absent in Ph+ CML (B3). This results in a weak_for effect to B1 and weak_against to B3 due to atypical features."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Has the patient had baseline WBC or neutrophil count trends?", "Are there features of marrow fibrosis (e.g., dry TPs, extramedullary hematopoiesis)?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow biopsy for fibrosis", "JAK2/MPL/ CALR mutation testing to exclude other MPNs"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.7, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.78, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "severity"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.02055318908420128, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absent lymphoid blast morphology and confirmed Ph+ status definitively exclude Ph-negative lymphoid neoplasm, but do not address Ph+ ALL as a potential differential."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0064228715888129, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.008221275633680514, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["No prior CML history reduces the probability of chronic-phase relapse but does not exclude de novo CML-BC as the presenting phase for Ph+ disease."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "confirmed", "prior": 0.31979695431472077, "posterior": 0.25897018246093606, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["82% blasts in peripheral blood definitively excludes CML慢性期 (B3.1) based on WHO criteria, but does not fully distinguish from CML加速期 (B3.2) which might show marrow-based blast increases not fully mirrored hematically.", "Peripheral blast percentage >30% indicates a more aggressive transformation phase (B3.3) than typical accelerated-phase CML (B3.2) which manifests with marrow-based blast increases. Supports blast crisis over accelerated phase."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Prior history of CML (unremarkable PMH weakly supports this)", "Subacute progression pattern (vs acute de novo AML)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow morphology to confirm myeloid blasts ≥82% with clonal markers", "Serum BCR-ABL1 mutational analysis for resistance patterns"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.8, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts (secondary AML)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.02055318908420128, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Chronic Phase", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.017341753289794825, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["82% blasts in peripheral blood exceeds criteria for accelerated phase CML and confirms transformation to blast crisis, strengthening the link between BCR-ABL1 positivity and disease progression."]}, "B3.2": {"id": "B3.2", "label": "CML in Accelerated Phase", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.011561168859863219, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Peripheral blast count >30% with splenomegaly and basophilia aligns more with blast crisis (≥20% blasts in peripheral blood) than accelerated phase CML (<20% blasts), strongly favoring transformation."]}, "B3.3": {"id": "B3.3", "label": "CML in Blast Crisis", "parent": "B3", "level": 2, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.10279187817258884, "posterior": 0.13817909021308522, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["82% blasts in peripheral blood definitively excludes CML慢性期 (B3.1) based on WHO criteria, but does not fully distinguish from CML加速期 (B3.2) which might show marrow-based blast increases not fully mirrored hematically.", "Peripheral blast percentage >30% indicates a more aggressive transformation phase (B3.3) than typical accelerated-phase CML (B3.2) which manifests with marrow-based blast increases. Supports blast crisis over accelerated phase."], "evidence_against": ["Retinal manifestations typically occur in lymphoid/lymphomatous processes but may still occur in CML-BC at 10-15% frequency according to WHO registry data. This produces weak contradictory evidence between B1.2 and B2."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.3.1", "B3.3.2", "B3.3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Subacute onset in known CML? (patient PMH unremarkable, but Ph+ status supports CML)", "Are blasts >20% in bone marrow vs. peripheral smear? (current >82% periphery)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Confirm BCR-ABL1 mutational status (resistance to therapy?),", "Bone marrow aspirate confirming >20% blasts in myeloid lineage"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.9, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "phase_transformation"}, "B3.3.1": {"id": "B3.3.1", "label": "CML in Blast Crisis with Myeloid Lineage Predominance", "parent": "B3.3", "level": 3, "status": "live", "prior": 0.08223350253807107, "posterior": 0.11986619873906187, "danger": 0.78, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The Ph+ status combined with subacute pancytopenia suggests a transformation phase rather than a mixed lineage crisis, providing moderate evidence for CML-BC.", "Ph+ status with subacute presentation and basophilia are typical of CML, but the >30% peripheral blasts argue against accelerated phase, favoring blast crisis."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Peripheral blast morphology consistent with myeloid lineage", "Absence of lymphoid lineage markers on physical exam"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Flow cytometry for myeloid vs lymphoid markers", "Bone marrow aspirate to confirm lineage"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.6, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.98, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "management_pathway"}, "B3.3.2": {"id": "B3.3.2", "label": "CML in Blast Crisis with Mixed or Lymphoid Lineage Features", "parent": "B3.3", "level": 3, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.010279187817258884, "posterior": 0.009988849894921822, "danger": 0.82, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Peripheral smear showing left-shifted granulocytes supports myeloid lineage in CML-BC, which is consistent with the BCR-ABL1-driven biology observed in the case.", "82% blasts in peripheral blood exceeds criteria for accelerated phase CML and confirms transformation to blast crisis, strengthening the link between BCR-ABL1 positivity and disease progression."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is immunophenotyping showing both myeloid and lymphoid markers?", "Any blasts with lymphoblast morphology? (current smear shows left-shifted granulocytes)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Ph+ CML lineage-specific markers by FISH", "Cytogenetic analysis for lymphoid translocations"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.94, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "management_pathway"}, "B3.3.3": {"id": "B3.3.3", "label": "CML in Blast Crisis with Preexisting TKI Resistance Mutation", "level": 3, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.00832404157910152, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B3.3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}}, "frontier": ["B3.3.2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do Ph+ status and subacute pancytopenia support consideration of mixed lineage crisis in a patient with CML-BC features?", "result_summary": "The Ph+ status combined with subacute pancytopenia suggests a transformation phase rather than a mixed lineage crisis, providing moderate evidence for CML-BC.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "weak_against", "B3.3.1": "moderate_for", "B3.1": "strong_against", "B2": "weak_against"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the combination of Ph+ status and subacute presentation with basophilia insufficient to assign definite accelerated phase CML?", "result_summary": "Ph+ status with subacute presentation and basophilia are typical of CML, but the >30% peripheral blasts argue against accelerated phase, favoring blast crisis.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B3.2": "strong_against", "B3.3.1": "moderate_for", "B1.2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the peripheral blast percentage >30% combined with splenomegaly and basophilia argue against CML in accelerated phase?", "result_summary": "Peripheral blast count >30% with splenomegaly and basophilia aligns more with blast crisis (≥20% blasts in peripheral blood) than accelerated phase CML (<20% blasts), strongly favoring transformation.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B3.2": "strong_against", "B3.3.1": "neutral", "B1.1": "weak_for"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of lymphoid blast morphology on peripheral smear rule out Ph-negative lymphoid neoplasm as a possible differential?", "result_summary": "Absent lymphoid blast morphology and confirmed Ph+ status definitively exclude Ph-negative lymphoid neoplasm, but do not address Ph+ ALL as a potential differential.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B2": "moderate_for", "B4": "moderate_against", "B3.3.2": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 82% peripheral blood blasts definitively exclude acceleration and instead confirm transformation to blast crisis?", "result_summary": "82% blasts in peripheral blood exceeds criteria for accelerated phase CML and confirms transformation to blast crisis, strengthening the link between BCR-ABL1 positivity and disease progression.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B3.1": "strong_against", "B3.3.1": "neutral", "B3.3.2": "weak_for"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 6, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of a documented prior chronic phase CML history in PMH confirm that this is not a chronic phase CML in relapse?", "result_summary": "No prior CML history reduces the probability of chronic-phase relapse but does not exclude de novo CML-BC as the presenting phase for Ph+ disease.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B2": "neutral", "B3.3.3": "neutral", "B1.1": "moderate_against"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.4721311475409837, "B2": 0.01639344262295082, "B3": 0.4131147540983606, "B4": 0.06557377049180328, "B5": 0.03278688524590164, "B1.1": 0.05245901639344264, "B1.2": 0.3672131147540984, "B1.3": 0.05245901639344264, "B3.1": 0.17704918032786884, "B3.2": 0.1180327868852459, "B3.3": 0.1180327868852459}, {"B1": 0.3578680203045685, "B2": 0.006345177664974619, "B3": 0.07138324873096445, "B4": 0.025380710659898477, "B5": 0.007931472081218274, "B1.1": 0.01269035532994924, "B1.2": 0.31979695431472077, "B1.3": 0.02538071065989848, "B3.1": 0.04282994923857867, "B3.2": 0.028553299492385786, "B3.3": 0.10279187817258884, "B3.3.1": 0.08223350253807107, "B3.3.2": 0.010279187817258884, "B3.3.3": 0.010279187817258884}, {"B1": 0.28774464717881787, "B2": 0.004110637816840256, "B3": 0.16708201236274325, "B4": 0.02055318908420128, "B5": 0.0064228715888129, "B1.1": 0.008221275633680514, "B1.2": 0.25897018246093606, "B1.3": 0.02055318908420128, "B3.1": 0.017341753289794825, "B3.2": 0.011561168859863219, "B3.3": 0.13817909021308522, "B3.3.1": 0.11986619873906187, "B3.3.2": 0.009988849894921822, "B3.3.3": 0.00832404157910152}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "Case features are consistent with a subacute hematologic syndrome without evidence of immediate life-threatening instability (e.g., no airway compromise, severe respiratory insufficiency, hypotension, or uncontrolled hemorrhage).", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "confirmation", "reason": "Root posterior (0.85) ≥ 0.75, but dangerous alternative B3.3 (posterior=0.118 ≥ 0.10) requires further differentiation. Confirmation would require resolving remaining high-impact differentials."}, "turn_budget_used": 3, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.75, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.25897018246093606, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_vignette": "A 52-year-old male presents to the emergency department with progressive fatigue,\nnight sweats, abdominal fullness, and blurred vision over the past 3 weeks. Past\nmedical history is unremarkable except for well-controlled hypertension.\n\nPhysical exam reveals:\n- Massive splenomegaly (8 cm below costal margin)\n- Bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots on fundoscopy\n- Scattered petechiae on lower extremities\n\nLaboratory findings:\n- WBC: 145,000/μL with 82% blasts\n- Hemoglobin: 7.2 g/dL\n- Platelets: 28,000/μL\n- Basophilia: 8%\n- LDH: 2,450 U/L (elevated)\n- Uric acid: 11.2 mg/dL (elevated)\n- Peripheral smear: left-shifted granulocytes at all stages of maturation\n\nCytogenetics / Molecular studies:\n- Philadelphia chromosome (Ph) positive\n- BCR-ABL1 fusion gene detected (p210 transcript)\n", "static_question": "What is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia - Blast Crisis (CML-BC)"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS)"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL)"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL)"}], "static_evidence_items": [{"id": "E1", "kind": "direct", "content": "Chief complaint: progressive fatigue, night sweats, abdominal fullness, blurred vision for 3 weeks", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E2", "kind": "direct", "content": "Past medical history: well-controlled hypertension", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E3", "kind": "direct", "content": "Physical exam finding: massive splenomegaly (8 cm below costal margin)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E4", "kind": "direct", "content": "Physical exam finding: bilateral retinal hemorrhages with cotton-wool spots on fundoscopy", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E5", "kind": "direct", "content": "Physical exam finding: scattered petechiae on lower extremities", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E6", "kind": "direct", "content": "WBC count: 145,000/μL with 82% blasts", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E7", "kind": "direct", "content": "Hemoglobin: 7.2 g/dL", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E8", "kind": "direct", "content": "Platelet count: 28,000/μL", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E9", "kind": "direct", "content": "Basophilia percentage: 8%", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E10", "kind": "direct", "content": "LDH level: 2,450 U/L (elevated)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E11", "kind": "direct", "content": "Uric acid level: 11.2 mg/dL (elevated)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E12", "kind": "direct", "content": "Peripheral smear finding: left-shifted granulocytes at all stages of maturation", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E13", "kind": "direct", "content": "Cytogenetics finding: Philadelphia chromosome (Ph) positive", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E14", "kind": "direct", "content": "Molecular finding: BCR-ABL1 fusion gene detected (p210 transcript)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'leukemia', 'lymphoma', 'pica', 'hemorrhage'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=25%, source=dxs]\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis: chronic myelogenous leukemia, bcr-abl1 positive\n\n[RAG context for 'abdominal fullness' (score=0.67):]\n  Source: Etiology of Acute Leukemia: A Review. > Diagnostic Tests\n  These morphological features are instrumental in distinguishing between lymphoid and myeloid blasts and further classifying them into specific subtypes, such as B-ALL, T-ALL, AML with maturation, or A\n[RAG context for 'abdominal fullness' (score=0.67):]\n  Source: The 2016 revision to the World Health Organization classification of myeloid neoplasms and acute leukemia. > Introduction\n  Acute vs chronic myeloid leukemia: Blasts, which are immature and dysfunctional cells, normally make up 1% to 5% of marrow cells. Acute leukemias are characterized by greater than 20% blasts on periph\n[RAG context for 'and blurred vision over the past 3 weeks' (score=0.70):]\n  Source: Pathology_Robbins\n  In addition, all myeloproliferative neoplasms have variable propensities to transform to a “spent phase” resembling primary myelofibrosis or to a “blast crisis” identical to acute leukemia, both presu\n[RAG context for 'and blurred vision over the past 3 weeks' (score=0.70):]\n  Source: The 2008 World Health Organization classification system for myeloproliferative neoplasms: order out of chaos. > Complications\n  Chronic myeloid leukemia (CML): CML patients if not treated are at increased risk of blast transformation.\n[Indirect reasoning chains (clinical inference):]\n  abdominal fullness → massive splenomegaly → Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis\n    (frequency: frequent)\n    Suggestion: Assess whether the abdominal fullness is secondary to massive splenomegaly, which aligns with the CML-BC phenotype and supports the candidate diagnosis\n  blurred vision over the past 3 weeks → leukostasis syndrome → Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis\n    (frequency: occasional)\n    Suggestion: Evaluate retinal imaging findings (hemorrhages/cotton-wool spots) for leukostasis syndrome, which would strongly implicate CML-blast crisis in this thrombocytopenic, pancytopenic leukemic pattern\n\nWhen indirect_reasoning_chains are present, generate candidates that investigate the INTERMEDIATE phenotype to confirm or rule out the indirect association."}
